an8.28:6.5 | S: This is a power that a mendicant who has ended the defilements relies on to claim: | T: The fact that the noble eightfold path is developed, well-developed by a monk whose effluents are ended is also is a strength of a monk whose effluents are ended, with reference to which he affirms the ending of the effluents (thus):
an8.28:6.6 | S: ‘My defilements have ended.’ | T: ‘The effluents are ended in me.’
an8.28:7.1 | S: A mendicant who has ended the defilements possesses these eight powers that qualify them to claim: | T: “These, lord, are the eight strengths of a monk whose effluents are ended, endowed with which he affirms the ending of the effluents (thus):
